🚀 Installation & Setup
1. Clone the Repository


git clone https://github.com/faizal-khan-a/CKD-Prediction-Web-App.git

Move into the project directory:



cd CKD-Prediction-Web-App
2. Create a Virtual Environment


python -m venv venv
3. Activate the Virtual Environment

For Windows PowerShell:



venv\Scripts\activate

If PowerShell blocks script execution:



Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy Bypass
venv\Scripts\activate
4. Install Dependencies

Install the packages listed in requirements.txt:



pip install -r requirements.txt

The project dependencies include:



flask
flask_sqlalchemy
pandas
scikit-learn
joblib
pdfkit
flask-migrate
flask-mail
5. Run the Application

Start the Flask application using:



python app.py

The application will start on the local Flask server.

Open the application in your browser:



http://127.0.0.1:5000
📦 Important Project Files
app.py

The main Flask application file.

It handles the web application routes and connects the user interface with the Machine Learning model and database functionality.

models.py

Contains the database model definitions used by the application.

train_model.py

Contains the Machine Learning model training process.

model.pkl

Contains the saved trained Machine Learning model used for prediction.

check_model.py

Used to inspect and verify the features expected by the saved model.

CKD_Preprocessed.csv

Contains the prepared dataset used for the Machine Learning workflow.

requirements.txt

Contains the Python packages required to run the project.

📈 Project Outcome

The completed project demonstrates the integration of a Machine Learning model into a functional web application.

Instead of keeping the Machine Learning model as a standalone training script, the project connects the trained model with a Flask-based user interface.

The resulting application provides a complete workflow:

User Registration → Sign In → Clinical Data Entry → Machine Learning Prediction → Patient Record → PDF Report

The project therefore demonstrates practical experience across several areas:

Machine Learning
Python
Flask development
Database integration
Web application development
Model integration
Patient record management
PDF report generation
